description:
The proposal seeks the demolition of the existing rear storage structure associated with the off-licence premises at 6 Turnpike Lane and the subdivision of the site to facilitate the erection of a new single-storey 1-bedroom, 2-person self-contained dwelling together with associated cycle and refuse storage.

The proposed dwelling would be positioned to the rear of the existing commercial premises and would benefit from an independent pedestrian access route via the established rear access arrangement between the rear of No.18 Turnpike Lane and the side of No.2 Waldegrave Road.

The revised proposal has been designed to provide a high-quality compact residential unit with a compliant internal floor area of approximately 51.25sqm and a floor-to-ceiling height of approximately 2.8m.

The accommodation would comprise:

Entrance and circulation space;
Open-plan kitchen/living area;
One double bedroom;
Bathroom facilities;
Integrated storage provision.

The dwelling would benefit from multiple sources of natural daylight and ventilation through a combination of windows and rooflights serving the principal habitable rooms.

The proposal also includes:

Secure long-stay cycle parking for two bicycles;
Dedicated refuse and recycling storage;
Soft landscaping and urban greening measures;
Sustainable design features including photovoltaic panels and air source heat pump technology.

The development would retain the continued operation of the existing off-licence premises and maintain a dedicated escape route for the commercial unit independently from the residential accommodation.
